sys: no external dialog programs on Haiku

Sys_Dialog() forks and runs zenity, kdialog or xmessage. Haiku has none of
them, and in a program with a BApplication (SDL's) the forked child's
exit() after the failed exec stops in the debugger ("exit() called after
fork from a BApplication"): a crash alert on the screen, and the parent
waiting for that child forever in Sys_Exec(). An error during a quit left
the game alive this way.

On Haiku the message goes to stderr (it is on the console already) and the
answer is the one given when no dialog program is found.

--- a/code/sys/sys_unix.c
+++ b/code/sys/sys_unix.c
@@ -1111,6 +1111,15 @@
 	dialogCommandType_t     preferredCommandType = NONE;
 	int                     i;
 
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+	/* Haiku has none of these programs, and a forked child of a program with a BApplication (SDL's) must
+	 * not call exit(): libbe stops it in the debugger with a crash alert, and Sys_Exec() waits for it
+	 * forever. The message is on the console already; answer as when no dialog program is found. */
+	(void)session; (void)tried; (void)commands; (void)preferredCommandType; (void)i;
+	fprintf( stderr, "%s: %s\n", title, message );
+	return type == DT_YES_NO ? DR_NO : DR_OK;
+#endif
+
 	commands[ ZENITY ] = &Sys_ZenityCommand;
 	commands[ KDIALOG ] = &Sys_KdialogCommand;
 	commands[ XMESSAGE ] = &Sys_XmessageCommand;
